Restores each AI client's MCP config from the launch journal:
byte-identically from the hash-checked backup when the file still holds
exactly what the relay wrote, else by reversing ONLY the relay-owned
entries (a later edit is preserved, never clobbered). A config that
cannot be restored keeps its journal row and backup and is reported.

Works whether or not the relay is enabled (it is the recovery path for
a config left wrapped after the relay was switched off). It does not
change [mcp_relay].enabled: while the relay stays enabled the daemon
re-projects on its next start - `observer mcp-relay disable` keeps the
originals.

Usage:
  observer mcp unwrap [flags]

Flags:
      --config string   path to config.toml (default ~/.observer/config.toml)
  -h, --help            help for unwrap
